versibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Say how the pinning test gets past the marks-file read at test_git_metrics.py:254 when subprocess.run is stubbed (e.g., the stub writes a marks file for each commit, or the test wraps the real run and asserts on the kwargs it received).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4444,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'it monkeypatches `subprocess.run` to capture `input` and asserts it is `bytes` containing no `\\r`'","tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py:245 `marks = repo.parent / f\"{repo.name}.marks\"`","tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py:254 `by_mark = dict(line.split() for line in marks.read_text().splitlines())` runs right after subprocess.run, and only git fast-import --export-marks creates that file"],"finding":"The planned pinning test assumes _fast_import_history can run with subprocess.run replaced by a stub that only captures `input`. The helper then calls `marks.read_text()` on a file that only a real `git fast-import` writes, so with that stub it raises FileNotFoundError before returning.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f52a34b3c39293bc7","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing, bullet 1 / AC 'A test pins that the fast-import stream is sent as bytes with LF line endings'; tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py:245-255","norm_id":"n285389ce1e9df51c","priority":0.3056,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The implementer writes the stub as described; the helper raises FileNotFoundError at line 254 and the new test errors instead of checking the stream","The implementer wraps the call in pytest.raises or try/except to get past it, which hides other failures from the helper"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Wrap the real subprocess.run instead of replacing it: record kwargs['input'] and then call through to real git (git is already required by these tests). Then assert isinstance(captured, bytes) and b'\\r' not in captured, and still use the returned shas. Alternatively, have the stub write ':N <40-hex>' lines to the --export-marks path parsed from argv and return subprocess.CompletedProcess(args, 0, b'', b'').","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Say that the `subprocess.run` replacement in the new pinning test records `input` and then calls the real `subprocess.run`, so the marks file is written and `_fast_import_history` returns normally before the bytes/no-`\\r` assertion.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3555,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"it monkeypatches `subprocess.run` to capture `input` and asserts it is `bytes` containing no `\\r`\"","tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py:254: `by_mark = dict(line.split() for line in marks.read_text().splitlines())` runs right after the `subprocess.run` call","Elsewhere in the same file (lines 315-317), `counting_run` already records each call and then calls the real `subprocess.run`."],"finding":"The planned pinning test replaces `subprocess.run` to capture `input`. But after that call, `_fast_import_history` reads the marks file with `marks.read_text()` (line 254). If the stub only records the call, git never writes that file, so the helper raises FileNotFoundError before the test reaches its bytes/no-`\\r` assertion. The plan does not say whether the stub forwards to the real `subprocess.run` or whether the test expects that error.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5531b7f8fd85a2da","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — first bullet (monkeypatch capture test)","norm_id":"nb5f1c76b74c557fb","priority":0.2445,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer writes a stub that only captures the call. The test errors with FileNotFoundError on every platform, and the implementer has to rework it or wraps it in a broad try/except that weakens the test."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the Testing bullet, say the monkeypatched `subprocess.run` records `kwargs[\"input\"]` and then delegates to the real `subprocess.run` (the same pattern as `counting_run` in this file). The test then calls `_fast_import_history` on a small tmp repo and asserts that the captured input is `bytes` and contains no `b\"\\r\"`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Dispatch the Windows validation by filename (`gh workflow run test.yml --ref tmp/<branch>`), or confirm that 294845723 resolves to test.yml with `gh workflow view 294845723` before relying on it.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.658,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"`gh workflow run 294845723 --ref tmp/...`\"","search_files('294845723', .github) -> (no matches): Unverified evidence class","The Windows job is in .github/workflows/test.yml:260-291 (`sweep-windows`, `if: ... github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch'`), so dispatching by filename is unambiguous: Verified"],"finding":"The validation dispatch uses the numeric workflow ID `294845723`, but nothing in the repo shows that this ID is test.yml (the only workflow with the sweep-windows job). If the ID is wrong or stale, the dispatch fails or runs a different workflow, and the Windows AC cannot be met as written.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd907fed8920a2e6c","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section / AC 'The 2 tests pass in a Windows sweep dispatched on the change'","norm_id":"nea0c3ebf9bb7380e","priority":0.242,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The ID belongs to a different workflow, or is stale after test.yml was renamed or re-created, so the dispatch runs the wrong workflow or gets a 404 and no Windows run is recorded"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace `gh workflow run 294845723 --ref tmp/...` with `gh workflow run test.yml --ref tmp/<branch>`, then use `gh run list --workflow test.yml --branch tmp/<branch> --event workflow_dispatch` to find the run and record its ID.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.55,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the pin test captures only the call whose argv starts with ['git', 'fast-import']. Other calls pass through to the real subprocess.run. Assert isinstance(input, bytes), b'\\r' not in input, and that text/universal_newlines are not truthy.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E2","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.3937,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"it monkeypatches `subprocess.run` to capture `input` and asserts it is `bytes` containing no `\\r`\"","\"A unit test feeds `_fast_import_history`'s exact stream through a CRLF translation check\" — wording does not say how the fast-import call is singled out"],"finding":"The pin test is under-specified about which subprocess.run call it captures and what the stub returns. _fast_import_history may make other subprocess calls, such as git init or rev-parse. It may also read the marks file after fast-import. A blanket stub could break the helper or capture the wrong call's input.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd61c7dc8bed3e3e6","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing — first bullet (monkeypatch subprocess.run)","norm_id":"na1d055287b5ed480","priority":0.2063,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The helper calls `git init` through subprocess.run before fast-import. The stub records that call's input (None), so the assertion fails or checks the wrong call.","The stub returns None, and the helper then reads the --export-marks file, which does not exist, so the test errors out for an unrelated reason."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Wrap the real subprocess.run. When argv[:2] == ['git', 'fast-import'], record kwargs['input'] and kwargs.get('text'), then delegate to the real call so the helper still completes. Assert isinstance(captured_input, bytes), b'\\r' not in captured_input, and not captured_text.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reword AC1 as '[non-codebase] Windows sweep run <run-id/URL> on commit <sha> shows test_history_walk_cat_file_starts_do_not_grow_with_revisions and test_oracle_cap_change_events_compares_unsampled_adjacent_revisions PASSED (not skipped), recorded on the ticket'.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["F1","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5214,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"The 2 tests pass in a Windows sweep dispatched on the change, recorded here.\""],"finding":"The Windows-sweep criterion does not say what evidence to record or where. \"Recorded here\" names no run ID, URL, or commit SHA. The evidence lives outside the codebase, but the criterion is not tagged [non-codebase] and names no concrete attestation.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fec52fdbfa55448f7","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — first line","norm_id":"n09ef11877f8f406b","priority":0.0786,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer cannot tell whether the recorded run actually tested the fixed commit or included both test IDs."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"[non-codebase] Windows sweep (workflow 294845723) run <run id + URL> on the tmp branch at the change's commit SHA shows both named tests PASSED (not skipped); run id, SHA, and timestamp are recorded on the ticket.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na"